# Seeds for failure cases proptest has generated in the past. It is
# automatically read and these particular cases re-run before any
# novel cases are generated.
#
# It is recommended to check this file in to source control so that
# everyone who runs the test benefits from these saved cases.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What a `cc` line is, and what it is not
#
# It is a seed for the generator, not a recording of an edit sequence. A seed
# reproduces the ORIGINAL failing case; the comment records what that case
# SHRANK to, which is shorter and always was. And a seed decodes through the
# generator AS IT IS NOW — adding an arm to `arb_edit` re-maps the whole random
# stream, so a line recorded before that change regenerates something else
# entirely. Those are marked `found:`.
#
# BEFORE adding an arm to `arb_edit`, convert anything here that is load-bearing
# into a fixed-case test. Nothing here is: both lines below were produced by
# deliberately reverting the fix to check this property is not vacuous, and each
# has its own named pin.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- `found:` — both recorded against a deliberately reverted `decide_shell`,
#     which returned `ShellChoice::Ours` unconditionally (the pre-fix
#     behaviour). They pass against the shipped code and pin nothing on their
#     own; they are kept because they still exercise the generator.
